<h2 id="s1">1. About This Manual</h2>

<p>This manual explains how to use the DEEP ALGORITHMS IAM &amp; PAM Console from beginning to end. It assumes you have never seen the platform before. Every page is described in plain language, every button is named exactly as it appears on screen, and every task is written as a numbered list of steps you can follow in order.</p>

<h3>1.1 Who should read this</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>New administrators</strong> who will create users, grant access and review security activity.</li>
  <li><strong>Client teams</strong> evaluating or adopting the platform.</li>
  <li><strong>Auditors and reviewers</strong> who need to read access records and denial reports.</li>
</ul>

<h3>1.2 How to read the instructions</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Text in <strong>bold</strong> is something you can see and click on screen, such as a button or a tab.</li>
  <li>Text in <code>this style</code> is a value you type or copy, such as an identifier or a web address.</li>
  <li>Numbered lists are step-by-step procedures. Follow them from top to bottom.</li>
  <li>The first time a technical word appears, it is explained in a box like the one below. All terms are also collected in the Glossary at the end.</li>
</ul>

<div class="term"><strong>Console</strong> — the word used in this manual for the website itself: the set of web pages you sign in to in order to manage identity, access and security records.</div>

<h3>1.3 About the screenshots</h3>
<p>Every major page and important screen in this manual has a screenshot placeholder. If you are able to add screenshots of that page, that is ideal; otherwise the blank space below each placeholder line is reserved so that images can be inserted later without changing the layout of the document.</p>

<div class="shot">
  <span class="line">[Screenshot Placeholder: Insert screenshot of the Console sign-in page here]</span><br />
